ta","data":[{"unit":1,"title":189,"area":190,"prev":192,"next":195,"titles":197,"firmware":59},{"id":2,"title":3,"aliases":4,"area":13,"order":14,"path":15,"context":16,"summary":23,"status":24,"firmware":25,"facts":30,"procedures":74,"parameters":139,"related":140,"body":145,"sources":146,"official_url":34,"controls":154},"howto.song-with-brain","Recipe — sketch a song fast with the brain",[5,6,7,8,9,10,11,12],"brain song","write a song fast","chord progression with brain","auto transpose","key detection","brain routing","keep a track out of the brain","set the key by hand","howto",32,"knowledge/manual/units/howto/song-with-brain.md",{"modes":17,"screens":19},[18],"auxiliary",[20,21,22],"M1","M2","bar","Build a tiny loop — drums, a one- or two-note bassline, one chord — then record a progression on the brain's keyboard (`T1` in auxiliary mode) and the routed tracks transpose along; take a lead out of the routing on `M2`, and set the key by hand when detection gets it wrong.","current",{"min":26,"changed_in":27,"guide_version":28,"verified_on":29},"1.0.9",[],"1.1.15",null,[31,36,39,42,45,48,51,55,61,66,71],{"id":32,"text":33,"source":34,"firmware_min":29,"verified_on":29,"confidence":35},"start-small","Start in a new project with a drum beat, a bassline of one or two notes and one chord on a pad or pluck track, one or two bars long.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/how-to#write-a-song-fast-with-brain","official",{"id":37,"text":38,"source":34,"firmware_min":29,"verified_on":29,"confidence":35},"open","The brain is `T1` in auxiliary mode.",{"id":40,"text":41,"source":34,"firmware_min":29,"verified_on":29,"confidence":35},"scale-4","`bar + accidental 4` on the brain sets its track scale to 4, so its sequence runs four times slower and spans four bars.",{"id":43,"text":44,"source":34,"firmware_min":29,"verified_on":29,"confidence":35},"detect","The brain has already detected the key and scale of the recorded parts and shows them on screen.",{"id":46,"text":47,"source":34,"firmware_min":29,"verified_on":29,"confidence":35},"transpose","Notes played on the brain's keyboard transpose the routed tracks, chords included, so the simple loop follows a progression.",{"id":49,"text":50,"source":34,"firmware_min":29,"verified_on":29,"confidence":35},"exclude","Parts that must not transpose, such as a lead, come out of the brain's routing on `M2`: turn an encoder to add or remove its track, click to swap between tracks 1–4 and 5–8.",{"id":52,"text":53,"source":54,"firmware_min":29,"verified_on":29,"confidence":35},"detection-input","Only routed tracks feed the key detection.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/auxiliary#brain",{"id":56,"text":57,"source":58,"firmware_min":29,"verified_on":59,"confidence":60},"lead-track","In a new project the lead is `T5`, the dissolve preset lead/gaussian.","docs/research/30-presets-samples.md#11-a-new-projects-sounds","1.1.33","verified",{"id":62,"text":63,"source":64,"firmware_min":29,"verified_on":29,"confidence":65},"routed-by-default","A new project routes tracks 3–8 to the brain, the lead among them, and leaves the drum tracks 1 and 2 out.","docs/research/10-xy-format.md#34-patternstruct-base-clones-walking","community",{"id":67,"text":68,"source":69,"firmware_min":29,"verified_on":29,"confidence":70},"routing-turns","The routing page draws the tracks the brain hears as boxes 1–8; on the replica an encoder turned clockwise takes its track in and counter-clockwise takes it out, a direction the guide does not give.","docs/research/59-screen-profiling.md#213-auxiliary-tracks","derived",{"id":72,"text":73,"source":69,"firmware_min":29,"verified_on":59,"confidence":60},"by-hand","The brain's manual mode sits at the counter-clockwise end of `E1` (CC12 at 0 showed manual), and in manual `E2` sets the root and `E3` the scale.",[75,98,115],{"id":76,"goal":77,"preconditions":78,"steps":81,"result":97,"source":34,"firmware_min":29,"verified_on":29,"confidence":35},"progression","Turn a one-chord loop into a progression",[79,80],"a short loop of drums","bass and one chord plays",[82,85,92,94],{"keys":83,"note":84,"set":29},"auxiliary → T1","the brain",{"keys":86,"note":87,"set":88},"bar + accidental 4","four bars per brain sequence",{"param":89,"value":90,"area":22,"track":91},"track scale",4,9,{"keys":93,"note":29,"set":29},"record + play",{"keys":95,"note":96,"set":29},"keys","play the progression within the shown scale","The bass and the chord follow the progression; drums stay where they are.",{"id":49,"goal":99,"preconditions":100,"steps":101,"result":114,"source":34,"firmware_min":29,"verified_on":29,"confidence":35},"Keep the lead on `T5` out of the brain's transposition",[],[102,104,107],{"keys":21,"note":103,"set":29},"the brain's routing, tracks 1–4 on the encoders",{"keys":105,"note":106,"set":29},"click E1","tracks 5–8 on the encoders",{"keys":108,"note":109,"set":110},"turn E1","counter-clockwise, `T5` out",{"param":111,"value":112,"area":18,"track":91,"page":113},"track 5","out",2,"The lead keeps its notes while everything routed moves.",{"id":116,"goal":117,"preconditions":118,"steps":119,"result":138,"source":54,"firmware_min":29,"verified_on":29,"confidence":35},"key-by-hand","Set the brain to A minor by hand",[],[120,121,126,132],{"keys":20,"note":29,"set":29},{"keys":108,"note":122,"set":123},"counter-clockwise, manual",{"param":124,"value":125,"area":18,"track":91},"mode","manual",{"keys":127,"note":128,"set":129},"turn E2","root a",{"param":130,"value":131,"area":18,"track":91},"root","a",{"keys":133,"note":134,"set":135},"turn E3","scale minor",{"param":136,"value":137,"area":18,"track":91},"scale","minor","The brain's page reads a minor, and the routed tracks' step components move in that scale.",[],[141,142,143,144],"auxiliary.brain","sequencer.track-scale","howto.song-from-scenes","howto.first-chords","The brain does the harmony work: write simple parts in one key, then let the brain move them as you\nplay. Take any part that should stay put, such as a lead, out of its routing, and give the brain a\nkey by hand when it guesses wrong on a sparse loop. The progression can also be written rather than\nplayed: one note per chord change on the brain's own pattern, which at track scale 4 lasts four\ntimes as long as the loop. Once it works, arrange it into a song with scenes.",[147,149,150,152,153],{"url":34,"kind":148},"guide",{"url":54,"kind":148},{"url":58,"kind":151},"research",{"url":64,"kind":151},{"url":69,"kind":151},[155,156,157,158,159,160,161,162,163,164,165,166,167,168,169,170,171,172,173,174,175,176,177,178,179,180,181,182,183,184,185,186,187,188],"key.auxiliary","track.1","key.bar","keyboard.cs4","key.record","key.play","keyboard.f3","keyboard.fs3","keyboard.g3","keyboard.gs3","keyboard.a3","keyboard.as3","keyboard.b3","keyboard.c4","keyboard.d4","keyboard.ds4","keyboard.e4","keyboard.f4","keyboard.fs4","keyboard.g4","keyboard.gs4","keyboard.a4","keyboard.as4","keyboard.b4","keyboard.c5","keyboard.cs5","keyboard.d5","keyboard.ds5","keyboard.e5","key.m2","encoder.1","key.m1","encoder.2","encoder.3","Sketch a song fast with the brain",{"id":13,"title":191},"How-to recipes",{"id":193,"title":194},"howto.load-samples","Load samples from a computer",{"id":143,"title":196},"Build a song from scenes",{"basics.key-notation":198,"basics.main-modes":199,"basics.modules":200,"basics.track-buttons":201,"basics.linked-tracks":202,"basics.patterns-scenes-songs":203,"basics.workflow":204,"basics.firmware-versions":205,"hardware.layout":206,"hardware.power-and-charging":207,"hardware.connectors":208,"hardware.specifications":209,"hardware.te-boot":210,"hardware.firmware-update":211,"hardware.factory-reset":212,"hardware.system-menu":213,"hardware.safety-and-care":214,"hardware.in-the-box":215,"sequencer.overview":216,"sequencer.step-entry":217,"sequencer.step-recording":218,"sequencer.live-recording":219,"sequencer.extend-notes":220,"sequencer.nudge":221,"sequencer.single-sound":222,"sequencer.rotate